course: dictionary
lesson: 5526
title: One word, many meanings: leave
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: The word leave can mean different things, so the words around it are its context, and they tell you which meaning to use. «I left my bag at school.» Here left means you forgot it and it stayed behind, not that you walked out with it.
explain: «Leave me alone!» shouted at someone means stop bothering me. «Leave it to me» means I will do it. Read the rest of the sentence, then ask: what word would fit here? Try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Left can also be a direction, as in «Turn left at the big oak tree», which means the side opposite right. «Sick leave» is a noun meaning time off when you are poorly, and «leave to speak» means permission to talk.
fact: Leave (verb) means to go away from a place, as in «leave the room».
fact: To leave something is to let it stay where it is or to forget it: «I left my coat on the bus.»
fact: «Left» can mean still there after others have gone: «Two biscuits are left.»
fact: «Leave alone» means do not touch or bother: «Leave the cake alone until after tea.»
fact: Leave as a noun means time off or permission, and «leave a message» means to let someone know something by writing or saying it.
exercise: «If 6 of those 24 pencils are given away, 24 − 6 = 18 are left.» In this sentence, what does left mean? | Forgot about them | *Still there after some have gone | Turned to the left side | Went out of the room
exercise: «Leave me alone!» What does it mean? | Please wait for me | *Stop bothering me | Go away from the room | Come and play with me
exercise: «I left my bag at school.» What does left mean here? | Lost it on purpose | Carried it to the park | Took it home with me | *Forgot it, so it stayed behind
test: «Turn left at the big oak tree.» What does left mean? | Forgotten | Still remaining | Gone away | *The side opposite right
test: Sam asked his teacher for «leave to speak.» What does leave mean here? | Going out of the room | *Permission | Forgetting something | Time off school because he is ill
exam: Ella said «I'm off» and walked out of the door. What does «I'm off» mean? | I have lost my bag | *I am leaving | I am very hungry | I am going to bed
